# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheels/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# ── Virtualenvs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Local secrets / rendered env — never commit ──────────────────────────────
# Highest-consequence category: a leaked build artifact is noise, a leaked key is
# an incident. Deliberately broad — an over-broad rule here costs one `git add -f`,
# an under-broad one costs a rotation.
*.env
.env*
secrets.enc.yaml
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*
*.ppk
.netrc
.npmrc
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.crt
*.csr

# ── Local brain data / backups — never commit (data lives in XDG, not the repo) ─
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
braincell-backup-*.db
# Pre-merge snapshots written by `consolidate --apply` / `reflect --apply` (v5).
braincell-pre*-*.db
# SQLite WAL/shared-memory sidecars. `*.db` does NOT cover these, and a `-wal`
# holds committed-but-uncheckpointed PAGE DATA — i.e. real brain content — so
# leaving them unignored would leak exactly what `*.db` exists to keep out.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*-journal
# Fixed, reused BrainCell interprocess coordination files. These live beside
# XDG databases in normal operation, but must not become source artifacts if a
# developer redirects state into a checkout.
*.mutation.lock

# ── Tooling / caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# ── Editor / OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
# Windows counterparts — the macOS side was covered, this side was not.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Merge / backup leftovers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conflict and backup residue is a common accidental commit; none of it is source.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
# Dated backups — `*.bak` misses these because the suffix TRAILS the extension
# (e.g. settings.json.bak-2026-07-23), which is exactly how a hand-made
# pre-change copy tends to be named.
*.bak-*
*.bak.*
*.backup
*.backup-*
*.backup.*

# ── Internal working notes — keep LOCAL, never publish ───────────────────────
# Maintainer-only state (status flags, licensing/provenance strategy, deployment
# details). Maintained locally on the maintainer's machine and excluded from
# Git history. See each file for why it must not be public-facing.
CLAUDE.md
# Codex project instructions point at the internal CLAUDE.md and carry the same
# maintainer-only architecture/publishing state.
/AGENTS.md
# Internal planning / spec / review / design-mockup artifacts (root-level).
# These are working notes, not user-facing product docs — keep them local.
# (braincell-mcp-wrapper.sh is a shipped launcher, NOT matched by these.)
/braincell-*.md
/braincell-*.html
# CLAUDE.md progress-pointer doc — same "never committed" policy as CLAUDE.md itself.
/docs/STAGE_LOG.md
# Internal planning docs (same convention as STAGE_LOG) — a broad `git add docs/`
# must never track or publish them. The .html is the generated companion view
# (self-contained, multi-MB); same policy as the root-level /braincell-*.{md,html} pair.
/docs/*-plan-*.md
/docs/*-plan-*.html
# CLAUDE.md restructure spillover (internal status + licensing strategy) — keep local.
/docs/claude-md-pruned-2026-07-21.md
/docs/claude-md-pruned-2026-07-25.md
# Path-scoped area conventions (.claude/rules/*.md) + any other agent working state.
# Same class as CLAUDE.md — internal maintainer notes, not user-facing product docs —
# so they follow the same "never committed" policy. Git history cannot be retracted.
/.claude/

# Memory ON/OFF task A/B eval — harness + fixtures tracked; runtime artifacts ignored.
/evals/task-ab/*.log
/evals/task-ab/**/__pycache__/
